Adjudication: F-1, F-2, and F-4 are REAL. F-3 is RESOLVED-ALREADY by the acceptance record’s own scope qualifier and the theorem’s explicit clause-level perimeter. No finding is obstructed.

### F-1 — REAL

The frozen theorem asserts a single transport object, but the proof constructs only five heterogeneously typed faces. “ONE” cannot mean uniqueness—the character twist \(\widetilde E\mapsto\widetilde E\eta\) disproves that—and no common map with cross-face compatibility is constructed.

The honest consumed scope is a five-field anchored transport package. The face table proves that package by record assembly.

Verbatim-ready append:

