### F-2 — REAL

PE10’s \(H^1=0\) uniqueness claim is false for the ordinary trivial coefficient action. Nothing in either dated annex repairs it. This affects only the certification narrative, not WM-CLASS’s proved existence/class identity.

Verbatim-ready append:

> **[ANNEX 2026-08-12, correction C6 F-2 — withdrawal of PE10’s \(H^1=0\) uniqueness gloss.]** In the 2026-08-07 ACCEPTANCE RECORD, the phrase
>
> “the DIRECT-\(H^2\)/bar-resolution route proving \(\widetilde E\) is THE canonical gauge — constructed from the cocycle alone and forced by \(H^1=0\) uniqueness”
>
> is withdrawn and replaced by:
>
> “the DIRECT-\(H^2\)/bar-resolution route independently re-verifying the WM-CLASS cohomology-class identity; the displayed gauge is the explicit section gauge \(\widetilde E=E\circ\sigma\), determined relative to the already fixed weld cochain \(E\) and minimal-window section \(\sigma\), with no uniqueness-from-\(H^1\) claim.”
>
> **Derivation of the correction.** With the trivial action on \(K^\ast\),
> \[
> H^1(\mathbb Z/E,K^\ast)
>   =\operatorname{Hom}(\mathbb Z/E,K^\ast)
>   =\mu_E(K),
> \]
> which need not vanish. If \(F\) and \(G\) are two gauges with
> \(\partial F=\partial G\), put \(\eta=F/G\). Then
> \[
> 1=\frac{\partial F}{\partial G}
>   =\partial\eta,\qquad
> \frac{\eta(\nu)\eta(\nu')}{\eta(\nu+\nu')}=1,
> \]
> so \(\eta\) is a character. Conversely, for every character \(\eta\),
> \[
> \partial(F\eta)=(\partial F)(\partial\eta)=\partial F.
> \]
> Hence gauges with a fixed coboundary form a torsor under
> \(\operatorname{Hom}(\mathbb Z/E,K^\ast)\), rather than being unique. For
> \(E=2\) and \(K=\mathbf F_5\), the character
> \(\eta(\nu)=(-1)^\nu\) is already a nontrivial witness.
>
> WM-CLASS itself is unchanged: its proof uses the explicitly defined
> \(\widetilde E=E\circ\sigma\), WM-RHO, and
> \[
> \partial\widetilde E=\partial E\cdot\rho_T^\kappa,
> \]
> and requires neither reconstruction from \(c\) alone nor uniqueness.
>
> **Consumer sweep.** WM-CLASS’s display and S6/WM6 survive unchanged.
> DULEMMA’s use of the coboundary identity survives unchanged. WELD-M-PKG’s
> \(M3\) field asserts no gauge uniqueness. PE10’s corrected route remains
> an independent verification of the class identity only.

