### F-4 — REAL

WM-FENCE proves a criterion for fixed data, not freedom to alter the data until the criterion holds. The phrase “WM-FENCE’s (F-b)-freedom observation” therefore misattributes any required existence or variation theorem. The “through J-D0” qualification limits the blast radius but does not cure the attribution.

Verbatim-ready append:

> **[ANNEX 2026-08-12, correction C6 F-4 — J-D consumes an F-b criterion, not freedom supplied by WM-FENCE.]** The frozen S6 downstream-design clause
>
> “the J-D block … consumes WM-FENCE’s (F-b)-freedom observation only through the already-adjudicated (J-D0) route”
>
> is replaced by:
>
> “the J-D block (J-D0 \(\to\) W-10 at the \((2,1,1)\) shape \(\to\) W-11) may consume WM-FENCE only as the fixed-data (F-b) character-triviality criterion, and only through the already-adjudicated J-D0 route. WM-FENCE supplies no freedom or existence theorem for varying \(z_\mu\), \(A_\mu\), the attained set, or the representative. Any such choice or variation required by J-D must be proved by J-D0 independently.”
>
> **Derivation.** For the fixed data, WM-FENCE proves exactly
> \[
> \chi_i^{(\mu)}=1\ \forall i\in\mathbb Z
> \iff \operatorname{ord}(z_\mu)\mid A_\mu
> \]
> in the absolute form, and
> \[
> \chi_i^{(\mu)}=1\ \forall i\in e_\mu\mathbb Z
> \iff \operatorname{ord}(z_\mu)\mid e_\mu A_\mu
> \]
> in the slot-grid form. Neither display contains an existential
> quantifier over the fixed inputs. For example, with
> \(K_\mu=\mathbf F_5\), \(z_\mu=2\), \(\operatorname{ord}(z_\mu)=4\),
> \(A_\mu=1\), and attained set containing \(1\),
> \[
> \chi^{(\mu)}_1=2^{-1}\ne1,
> \]
> so absolute PERIM fails, and WM-FENCE specifies no operation that changes
> this datum.
>
> **Consumer sweep.** WM-FENCE(a), (b), and (c), including the
> root-inclusive repair and the \(\chi\)-chain/mod-wrap caveats, survive
> unchanged. The correction touches only the unexecuted S6 J-D design
> sentence. No executed downstream consumption identified at HEAD relies
> on an WM-FENCE freedom theorem. A future J-D proof must cite J-D0 for any
> required existence or variation and WM-FENCE only to test the resulting
> character-triviality condition.

